  "question": {
    "text": "Positive and negative point charges of equal magnitude are kept at $\\left(0,0, \\frac{a}{2}\\right)$ and $\\left(0,0, \\frac{-a}{2}\\right)$, respectively. The work done by the electric field when another positive point charge is moved from $(-a, 0,0)$ to $(0, a, 0)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6pv0j",
      "text": "\npositive\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "YZEoy",
      "text": "\nnegative\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8jLXi",
      "text": "\nzero\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "vg8pE",
      "text": "\ndepends on the path connecting the initial and final positions",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$A \\equiv(-a, 0,0) B \\equiv(0, a, 0)$\nPoint charge is moved from $A$ to $B$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nV_A & =V_B=0 \\\\\nW & =0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$$\n\\therefore \\quad W=0\n$$\nor the correct option is (c).\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/DiaY3X6xlxWW2TjNqO0u9R-XGUrorZAnreRtLsMUkok.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
